ORIENTATION PROOF: edge k=i*N+j has edge_index[0]=i (source), edge_index[1]=j (target),
weight E[i,j]. PyG flow='source_to_target' gathers x_j:=x[edge_index[0]] and scatters
into out[edge_index[1]]. Hence out[j] = sum_i E[i,j] x_i = (E^T X)[j].
For SYMMETRIC real FC E^T==E so this is invisible; for a learned asymmetric Bernoulli
mask it is NOT. RECORD FOR S8.

