max|True - False| = 2.000000  -> ReLU is NOT a no-op here

worked example: negative x times negative FC, edge u=1 -> v=0, E[1,0]=0.25
  x_1 = [-0.5, 3.0]  (component 0 is negative)
  A (relu=False): e*x_u        = [-0.125, 0.75]
  B (relu=True) : e*relu(x_u)  = [0.0, 0.75]
  => with relu=False a negative feature times a positive/negative edge keeps its sign
     and can ADD positively; with relu=True the negative component is zeroed BEFORE
     weighting, so it contributes nothing regardless of edge sign.

